# Two identities, deliberately.
#
# GitHub never counts a pull request author's own review. Agent-authored PRs in
# this estate are authored by one identity, while a CODEOWNER approval is
# required to merge — so a CODEOWNERS naming only the author identity produces a
# repository whose own PRs can never be approved.
#
# Admin permission is NOT code ownership; it does not satisfy the requirement.
* @mw-aqa @mw-io
